From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:40:41 +0000
Subject: Hold navigations until ad blocking filter lists are read

Requests are checked against the filter lists that are loaded when the
request starts. At startup the installed lists are read from disk on a
worker thread, and a tab restored at startup, a link opened from another
app or a custom tab could start loading before that read finished. Its
page and the requests the page made were then not filtered.

Defer HTTP and HTTPS navigations, in every profile including
off-the-record ones, until every enabled filtering configuration has read
its installed lists. The subscription service reports this through
IsInitialized() and RunWhenInitialized(). Navigations that start later
are not throttled. A navigation waits at most 5 seconds; after that it
goes ahead and a warning is logged.

